arxiv-2407-15827.description:
A 2024 arXiv research paper by Ilya Krishtal and Brendan Miller. We extend the classical Kadec 1 4 \frac{1}{4} theorem for systems of exponential functions on an interval to frames and atomic decompositions formed by sampling an orbit of a vector under an isometric group representation. Introduction and main results

The celebrated Kadec
\frac{1}{4}
theorem
[
14
]
states that a system of exponential functions
\{\mathbf{e}_{\mu_{n}}:n\in{\mathbb{Z}}\}
, where
\mathbf{e}_{\mu_{n}}(t)=e^{i\mu_{n}t}
,
t\in(-\pi,\pi)
, is a Riesz basis (see Definition
3.1
) for the Hilbert space
{\mathcal{H}}=L^{2}(-\pi,\pi)
provided that
\delta=\sup\{|\mu_{n}-n|:n\in{\mathbb{Z}}\}<\frac{1}{4}
.
